		<td width="150" align="left" valign="top" class="row1"><span class="name"><a name="11993"></a><b>Mreow/Stepwolf</b></span><br /><span class="postdetails"><br /><img src="images/avatars/gallery/Avatar_pack_1/080.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br /><br />Joined: 12 Aug 2004<br />Posts: 1<br />Location: Waiting for the PKs to zone in</span><br /></td>
		<td class="row1" width="100%" height="28" valign="top"><table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=11993&amp;sid=cbfb21e04e9bd14dd0fc0921390a13f3#11993"><img src="templates/Classic/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Thu Aug 12, 2004 12:58 pm<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: Eh, did you just say no more ganking?</span></td>
				<td valign="top" align="right" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=11993&amp;sid=cbfb21e04e9bd14dd0fc0921390a13f3"><img src="templates/Classic/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Lurker alert!  <img src="images/smiles/icon_eek.gif" alt="Shocked" border="0" /> 
<br />

<br />
I haven't really had time to digest this change, but at first glance I was a happy puppy.  Most (all but Stepwolf) of my 16 characters are twinked-out PK hunters (The only difference being that Step is in all No Drop already), and getting augs was teh drag!  My jaw literally dropped while browsing through the multitude of "Improvements" that will flip-flop the dynamics of RZ.  Not bagging my level 24, 255int casters will be hard to get used to.  I'm already envisioning the level of fearlessness I'll reach when inflicted with blindness and the like - I may develop blind fighting via my surround sound, rather than slamming on strafe-run, rolling up into a ball and hoping they haven't disarmed my recently purchased 50k weapon or notice the fungi.
<br />

<br />
I'm admittedly soured at the notion of them eliminating 95% of my prey: the Ganking PKs who took delight on griefing newbies and oldbies.  I mean, now I'll be relegated to hunting zone-in campers (what else would ganks turn into?), and they'll most likely find allies and form large groups (group pvp point bonus), which will inevitably result in my doom.  Lost are the days of the wandering solo PK.
<br />

<br />
Or are they <img src="images/smiles/icon_question.gif" alt="Question" border="0" />   I'm hopeful to still find abundant prey in the form of solitary stalkers, as I rarely choose to group when hunting (most everyone is more interested in hopping right back onto the exp treadmill if they can actually <span style="font-style: italic">get </span>a group).
<br />

<br />
A growing concern of mine is what will now define a PK.  Of course, the mainstay <span style="font-style: italic">bungholes</span> will forever be the griefing, training, mob-stealing scum of Norrath.  What caught me off guard is how much they're encouraging pvp, and if long-time 'Anti's will turn 'random PK' for no other reasons than 'you can't gank anymore' and 'everybody's doing it!'  I was immediately alarmed when I found my mind wandering through the possiblities of the point system and how much more lethal my 16dmg piercer would be.
<br />

<br />
Several players reach a temporary plateau, as I have many times, when the 20+ hours of exp grinding, corpse running, shouting for groups, and playing alts simply isn't worth 60 max hit points more (let alone $13).  My greatest fear lies in the possiblity that the majority of my kind would 'turn to the dark side' and (de)evolve the server into Super Sullon Smash Bros Melee (only without the level 65 epic rogues camping blackburrow and crushbone).  I've asserted and re-asserted my take on PKs ("No quarter shall be granted for the wicked!"), but those PKs simply don't exist anymore.
<br />

<br />
The light I once defended (saving everyone from having their hard-earned, real-life-time-spent equipment looted by an opportunist, real-life bastard) has had it's switch flipped to *OFF*, and here I'll stumble in the dark, trying to either find another light to follow until I eventually either give up and shut the door or start to see the world in a different light - likely seeking toward the more dastardly ranks for friendship.  Such a turn could possibly lead me down the path of dishonor, forever in pursuit of gaining the upper hand by any means necessary (low-hp griefers!)
<br />

<br />
Never, I say! <img src="images/smiles/icon_mad.gif" alt="Mad" border="0" />  Never would I imagine myself able to think such thoughts. (Nevermind the fact that I just thought them <img src="images/smiles/icon_lol.gif" alt="Laughing" border="0" />)  After all, PVP points can be earned honestly via slaying griefers/trainers/KSers.  So then, what's all the hubbub?  Maybe I'm just paranoid.  <img src="images/smiles/icon_sad.gif" alt="Sad" border="0" /> 
<br />

<br />
Time will tell!
<br />

<br />
Oh, "WOOF"  . . . or something<div style="vertical-align: bottom"><br /><br /><br />_________________<br />Signature? Should I write on teh screen here? I don't get it. /yell</div></span><span class="gensmall"></span></td>
			</tr>
